# Cenote Scout's ruling: "If no card is revealed, most likely because that player's library is empty, the exploring creature
# receives a +1/+1 counter." (CR 701.44a: if a land card is not revealed, the permanent gets the counter; CR 701.44b: it
# explores even though part of the process was impossible.) Bot1's whole deck is the seven cards of its hand, so its library is
# empty: the Scout is a 2/2, nothing is asked, nothing is revealed, and Bot1 has not lost (no draw has been tried).

